TAFF\nHealth Sciences Graduate Programs\nHome |\nHealth Sciences Graduate Programs\nHealth Sciences Graduate Programs\nPhD, Biomedical Research\nMD/PhD Dual Degree Program\nMS, Biomedical Research\nBS to PhD\nCertificate in Medical Science\nResearch Clusters\nResearch Faculty\nStudent Resources\nAmerican Heart Association Summer Internship\nGraduate Education Forms\nHealth Sciences Research Day\nInformatics & Population Analytics\nMarshall Journal of Medicine\nStudent Funding Opportunites\nStudent Organizations\nQuality & Safety Summit\nContact Us\nDrive Discovery. Advance Health.\nWhether you\u2019re seeking to launch your career in research or deepen your expertise in clinical practice or prepare for doctoral or health profession studies, our graduate programs in health sciences provide a strong foundation for success.\nOffered through the Joan C. Edwards School of Medicine, our programs are designed to equip future healthcare leaders, scientists and educators with the knowledge, skills and experience to make meaningful contributions in a wide range of health-related fields.\nMaster\u2019s and Doctoral Degree Programs\nChoose from master's and doctoral programs through the School of Medicine, including:\nDoctoral Programs\nDoctor of Philosophy in Biomedical Research (PhD): The PhD program is a research-based degree that does not depend solely on the accumulation of credit hours. Graduates from the program are in biomedical careers--employed by universities or research institutes, industry, state or federal governments, community colleges and in other health professions. Learn More\nDual Degree Programs\nMD-PhD: The Doctor of Medicine (MD) & Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Biomedical Research blends the discovery of new knowledge with clinical medicine at the intersection of science and medicine. Most graduates work as physician-scientists at medical schools, conducting disease-related research and applying the results to the treatment of patients. Our MD-PhD graduates offer unique perspective on both the basic science and clinical science behind disease. Learn More\nBS-PhD: The combined Bachelor of Science (BS) to Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) in Biomedical Research program allows talented high schoolers and undergraduate students to kick start their research careers. In this accelerated format, students can earn both degrees in just seven years, rather than the traditional eight to nine years it takes to complete them separately. Learn More\nMaster's Degree Programs\nMS in Biomedical Research (thesis): This program is for students interested in research and either want to strengthen their applications to PhD programs or have an interest in working as a technician in a research lab. The program provides hands-on experience at multiple methods, including bioinformatics. Learn More\nClinical and Translational Science (CTS MS) Learn More\nMS in Medical Sciences and Research Emphasis (non-thesis): This program is designed for students who wish to work in the medical environment in clinical trials and informatics or those who wish to strengthen their applications to medical school (Medical Sciences area of emphasis). Graduates of this program are largely employed in clinical trial management or matriculate to medical school. Learn More\nGraduate Certificate & Other Opportunities\nCertificate in Medical Science Program\nAmerican Heart Association Undergraduate Summer Internship\nTour Tomorrow Today\nStep into the heart of our graduate and professional programs with this immersive virtual tour\u2014explore labs, collaborative study spaces and campus landmarks. Discover how Marshall\u2019s vibrant community and state-of-the-art facilities can shape your future.\nABOUT US\nHistory\nNews\nMeet the Dean\nAccreditation\nEDUCATION\nMedical Education\nResidency Programs\nGraduate Medical Education\nContinuing Medical Education\nGraduate Education Programs\nRESEARCH\nCores & Initiatives\nBiomedical Sciences\nMarshall Journal of Medicine\nABOUT 